{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"The Phase D audit exposed one additional source-derived header shape that the initial “valid MP3 header” matrix had pruned too aggressively: the C code does not validate the two version bits or the 2-bit sample-rate code. That creates four reserved-version/table combinations plus the sample-rate-code-3 paths, including `sr_idx == 8`. Rust’s checked array indexing would abort on that last path while C stores the computed one-past table pointer. I’m expanding the matrix to all header combinations the C actually executes and changing Rust to compute those table pointers without a bounds check, matching the C boundary behavior."}}
